- role: assistant
  content: |
    Below is a concrete test plan for each phase with clear steps, expected results, and requirement IDs. Follow these sequentially; by the end, all requirements will be covered.

    **Pre‑Setup**
    - Start services: `docker compose up -d --build`
    - Frontend: http://localhost:8080
    - Backend (host): http://localhost:8800

    **Phase 0 Tests — Baseline Hardening**
    - Health endpoints
      - `curl http://localhost:8800/health` → 200, includes `status=ok`, `env`.
      - `curl http://localhost:8080/api/health` → 200, `{"status":"ok"}`.
    - Alembic
      - `docker compose exec backend alembic upgrade head` finishes with no errors.
    - Logs
      - `docker compose logs backend` show structured startup logs without tracebacks.
    - Requirements: none directly, foundational for all later phases.

    **Phase 1 Tests — AuthN + Roles (ACC-020, ACC-030, ACC-040, ACC-050)**
    - First owner login requires rotation (ACC-020)
      - Attempt login with default credentials at `/login` UI or `POST /api/auth/login`.
      - Expect redirect/block with “change password” form or `must_rotate_pw=true`.
      - `POST /api/auth/rotate-password` succeeds; repeat login works normally.
    - Owner can change credentials (ACC-030)
      - As owner, change username/password via profile UI or `PATCH /api/auth/me`.
      - Re-login works only with new credentials; old creds fail.
    - Admin manages admins and viewers (ACC-040, ACC-050)
      - As owner/admin, create another admin and a viewer via UI or `/api/admin/users`.
      - Deactivate/reactivate a user; verify inactive cannot log in.
      - Verify viewer can browse dashboards but receives 403 on write endpoints (devices, groups).
    - Cookie & session
      - Inspect cookie flags (HttpOnly present, SameSite=Strict in prod).
      - `GET /api/auth/me` returns current user; `POST /api/auth/logout` clears session.

    **Phase 2 Tests — Devices & Groups (CONF-010, CONF-020, CONF-030)**
    - Devices CRUD (CONF-010, CONF-020)
      - Create device with: name, location, unit, sampling interval, warn thresholds.
      - Update and delete device; confirm entries in audit history (UI panel or `GET /api/audit?...`).
      - Attempt write as viewer; expect 403.
    - Groups CRUD and assignment (CONF-030)
      - Create group(s), assign/unassign devices.
      - Rename/delete group; assignments update accordingly.
    - Data validation
      - Sampling interval > 0 enforced; thresholds can be null or numeric; invalids rejected.

    **Phase 3 Tests — Ingestion & Scheduler (DAT-010)**
    - DB readiness
      - Ensure TimescaleDB/Postgres is running; `alembic upgrade head` creates readings table/hypertable.
    - Polling
      - Configure test device(s) with reachable Modbus endpoint (or simulator).
      - Use “Test Connection” (UI) or `POST /api/devices/:id/test-connection`:
        - Success returns connectivity info (latency, basic read).
      - Start scheduler; verify per-device jobs registered (logs show job scheduling).
    - Persistence (DAT-010)
      - Wait > 2× sampling interval; query readings:
        - UI history quick glance, or `GET /api/readings?device_id=...&from=...&to=...`.
        - DB check (optional): `SELECT count(*) FROM readings WHERE device_id=...`.
      - Restart containers; data remains available (persistence confirmed).

    **Phase 4 Tests — Realtime Monitoring (LIV-010, LIV-020, LIV-030)**
    - WebSocket connectivity
      - Open live view and select multiple devices; charts begin updating automatically (LIV-010).
      - Dev-tool WS frames show JSON messages per device; frequency ~ sampling interval.
    - Threshold overlay (LIV-020)
      - Charts render warn_low/high as horizontal guides.
    - Exceed threshold highlighting (LIV-030)
      - Drive device reading beyond thresholds (simulator or injected test).
      - Chart segments display yellow (caution) and red (critical) overlay/segment styling.

    **Phase 5 Tests — Historical & Export (HIS-010, HIS-020)**
    - Historical trends (HIS-010)
      - Pick device and custom time range; chart renders data with reasonable bucket size.
      - Change range (last 1h/24h/custom) and verify performance and accuracy.
    - CSV export (HIS-020)
      - Click “Export CSV” for the selected device/range.
      - File downloads; open and confirm headers, timestamps, and values match UI/DB.

    **Phase 6 Tests — Group Dashboards (CONF-040)**
    - Group-scoped views (CONF-040)
      - Select a device group; live dashboard shows only assigned devices.
      - Switch to “History” tab; historical charts and export scope to group devices.
      - Assign/unassign a device; refresh view; membership reflected correctly.

    **Phase 7 Tests — Localization & UI (UI-010, UI-020, UI-030)**
    - Language switch (UI-010)
      - Toggle EN/中文 in header; strings update immediately with no reload.
      - Refresh page; last language persists.
    - Layout (UI-020)
      - Resize browser or use dev tools; dashboards remain readable and well-structured.
    - Transitions (UI-030)
      - Navigate between views; animations are smooth and subtle (no disruptive motion).

    **Phase 8 Tests — Hardening & Ops (ACC-010, DAT-010)**
    - Browser access (ACC-010)
      - Verify modern desktop browsers (Chrome/Edge) access without extra software.
    - Security and reliability
      - In prod mode, cookies have `Secure` (under HTTPS), `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`.
      - Rate of WS/API under moderate load is stable; logs include request IDs; errors are structured.
    - Health & startup
      - Compose healthchecks pass; services restart cleanly; data intact (DAT-010).

    **Requirements Coverage**
    - Concepts
      - DDMS-CON-010: Verified in ACC-010 tests and overall browser delivery.
      - DDMS-CON-020/030: Realized via devices and groups models (Phase 2) and dashboards (Phase 6).
    - Access & Authentication
      - DDMS-ACC-010: Phase 8 (modern browser access, no extra software).
      - DDMS-ACC-020: Phase 1 (first login requires password change).
      - DDMS-ACC-030: Phase 1 (owner updates username/password).
      - DDMS-ACC-040: Phase 1 (admin manages administrators).
      - DDMS-ACC-050: Phase 1 (read-only users; view-only permissions).
    - Live Monitoring & Alerts
      - DDMS-LIV-010: Phase 4 (concurrent real-time charts).
      - DDMS-LIV-020: Phase 4 (warning threshold markers).
      - DDMS-LIV-030: Phase 4 (yellow/red highlights when exceeded).
    - Historical Analysis & Export
      - DDMS-HIS-010: Phase 5 (historical trend charts for any range).
      - DDMS-HIS-020: Phase 5 (CSV export of displayed dataset).
    - Device & Group Configuration
      - DDMS-CONF-010: Phase 2 (add devices with all fields).
      - DDMS-CONF-020: Phase 2 (edit/delete with audit trail).
      - DDMS-CONF-030: Phase 2 (create/edit/delete groups and assignments).
      - DDMS-CONF-040: Phase 6 (group-scoped live/historical interfaces).
    - Localization & UI
      - DDMS-UI-010: Phase 7 (English/Chinese switch without reload).
      - DDMS-UI-020: Phase 7 (clean responsive layout).
      - DDMS-UI-030: Phase 7 (subtle dynamic effects).
    - Data Persistence
      - DDMS-DAT-010: Phases 3 and 8 (readings, accounts, and configs persisted across restarts).

    If helpful, I can turn these into checklist issues in GitHub with test commands and expected results attached, and wire the first test suites (auth flow and device CRUD) to start automation.
